---
// src/pages/share/wyoming-voters-choose/sources.astro
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Sources: Wyoming Voters Should Choose -- Skovgard 2026"
  description="Primary sources and research notes supporting the Wyoming Voters Should Choose share message about the Wyoming GOP bylaw fight and pre-primary endorsements."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="pt-20">

    <!-- Breadcrumb bar -->
    <div class="bg-wy-bone border-b border-gray-200 py-3 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest">
        <a href="/share" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-wy-ember transition-colors">All messages</a>
        <span class="text-gray-300">/</span>
        <a href="/share/wyoming-voters-choose/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-wy-ember transition-colors">Wyoming Voters Should Choose</a>
        <span class="text-gray-300">/</span>
        <span class="text-wy-charcoal">Sources</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="bg-wy-charcoal py-14 px-4 text-center">
      <p class="text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-3">Research Notes</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-serif font-extrabold text-wy-bone mb-4 leading-tight">
        Wyoming Voters Should Choose
      </h1>
      <p class="text-wy-bone/70 text-lg max-w-xl mx-auto">
        Sources and research notes supporting the claims in the share message.
        This is a research aid, not a legal opinion.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Preamble -->
    <section class="bg-wy-bone border-b border-gray-200 py-10 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl px-6 py-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            <strong>About this page.</strong> This page documents the primary sources behind the
            Wyoming Voters Should Choose share message. The central factual claim is that the
            Wyoming Republican Party adopted bylaws reserving the right to endorse, oppose, and
            financially support candidates before the primary election. The concern is that voters
            should choose nominees in the primary before party money and party machinery favor one
            candidate over another. The sources below document the bylaw language and the coverage
            of this issue.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Claims and support -->
    <article class="bg-wy-bone py-12 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto sources-content">

        <h2>Key claims and source support</h2>

        <div class="claims-table" role="table" aria-label="Claims and source support">
          <div class="claims-header" role="row">
            <span role="columnheader">Public statement</span>
            <span role="columnheader">Source support</span>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              The Wyoming GOP adopted a bylaw reserving the right to endorse, oppose, and financially
              support candidates before the primary election.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              Wyoming Republican Party bylaws (2024 or 2025 convention). The exact text from the
              bylaw states the party and its central committees reserve the "absolute First Amendment
              right to endorse, support, oppose, and provide financial assistance to candidates of
              its choosing at any point in the election cycle, including prior to a primary election."
              See source link below.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              Pre-primary party endorsements and spending disadvantage candidates who have not
              aligned with the faction in control.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              WyoFile has reported on the Wyoming GOP's pre-primary activity and internal faction
              fights. See TODO link below for the specific article.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="claims-row" role="row">
            <div role="cell">
              The pattern described -- centralizing power, reducing local control, loyalty screens --
              is visible in party and legislative activity over the 2024-2026 period.
            </div>
            <div role="cell">
              Community Chatter opinion by Shurie Scheel covers the insider-control concern from a
              local Wyoming perspective. See TODO link below.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>The bylaw excerpt</h2>

        <blockquote class="bylaw-block">
          "The Wyoming Republican Party, through its State and County Central Committees, reserves
          the absolute First Amendment right to endorse, support, oppose, and provide financial
          assistance to candidates of its choosing at any point in the election cycle, including
          prior to a primary election."
        </blockquote>

        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          <strong>Plain-English explanation:</strong> This bylaw language means the party structure --
          not rank-and-file voters -- can officially back or oppose a candidate with money and
          endorsements before a single vote is cast in the primary. The concern is that voters should
          choose nominees without the party machinery having already picked a winner. When the party
          spends against a candidate before the primary, voters are choosing on an uneven field.
        </p>

        <h2>Primary sources</h2>

        <div class="source-list">

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              Wyoming Republican Party Bylaws
              <span class="source-desc">Pre-primary endorsement and financial support provision</span>
            </p>
            <!-- TODO: Replace with verified URL to the adopted Wyoming GOP bylaw document (convention materials or official party website) -->
            <a href="#TODO-wyoming-gop-bylaws"
               class="source-link todo-link">
              TODO: Wyoming GOP convention bylaw materials (Jimmy to replace with verified link)
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Use the official adopted bylaw document. The exact language quoted above should be
              confirmed against the final adopted version from the most recent convention.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              WyoFile -- Wyoming GOP pre-primary endorsements
              <span class="source-desc">Reporting on party faction activity and pre-primary spending</span>
            </p>
            <!-- TODO: Replace with verified WyoFile article URL on Wyoming GOP pre-primary endorsements -->
            <a href="#TODO-wyofile-article"
               class="source-link todo-link">
              TODO: WyoFile reporting on Wyoming GOP pre-primary endorsements (Jimmy to replace with verified link)
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Use the specific WyoFile article that covers the bylaw fight or pre-primary endorsement
              activity. Do not substitute a general WyoFile homepage link.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="source-item">
            <p class="source-label">
              Community Chatter -- Shurie Scheel opinion
              <span class="source-desc">Local Wyoming perspective on insider control of the primary process</span>
            </p>
            <!-- TODO: Replace with verified URL to the Shurie Scheel Community Chatter piece -->
            <a href="#TODO-community-chatter-scheel"
               class="source-link todo-link">
              TODO: Community Chatter opinion by Shurie Scheel (Jimmy to replace with verified link)
            </a>
            <p class="source-note">
              Use the specific published piece. Confirm the author name and publication before linking.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <h2>Notes for responsible use</h2>

        <ul class="responsible-list">
          <li>The bylaw language quoted above should be confirmed against the final adopted version before public attribution. Party bylaws can be amended at conventions.</li>
          <li>Distinguish between a bylaw that reserves a right and actual pre-primary spending or endorsements. Both are worth documenting separately.</li>
          <li>Use "appears to," "claims the right to," or "reserves the right to" when describing the bylaw until the exact adopted text is independently verified.</li>
          <li>WyoFile and Community Chatter are secondary sources. The official party document or FEC/state disclosure filings are the primary sources for any spending claims.</li>
          <li>Do not describe this as illegal -- it may or may not raise legal questions. Describe it as a concern about fairness in the primary process and voter choice.</li>
        </ul>

      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Back CTA -->
    <div class="bg-white py-12 px-4 border-t border-gray-200 text-center">
      <a href="/share/wyoming-voters-choose/"
         class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-wy-ember text-wy-bone font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-wy-ember-dark transition-colors text-sm">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Wyoming Voters Should Choose
      </a>
    </div>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .sources-content { line-height: 1.75; color: #2b2b2b; }
  .sources-content h2 {
    font-family: 'Bitter', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    color: #2b2b2b;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #c68a4a;
  }
  .sources-content h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  .claims-table {
    border: 1px solid #ddd8ce;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .claims-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr;
    background: #2b2b2b;
    gap: 0;
  }
  .claims-header span {
    padding: 10px 16px;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: #f1ece1;
  }
  .claims-header span:first-child { border-right: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12); }
  .claims-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd8ce;
  }
  .claims-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .claims-row div {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #2b2b2b;
  }
  .claims-row div:first-child {
    background: #f1ece1;
    border-right: 1px solid #ddd8ce;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .claims-row div:last-child { background: #fafaf8; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .claims-header { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .claims-header span:first-child { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12); }
    .claims-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .claims-row div:first-child { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd8ce; }
  }

  .bylaw-block {
    background: #fefce8;
    border-left: 4px solid #c68a4a;
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #2b2b2b;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .source-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
    border: 1px solid #e5e2da;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .source-item {
    background: #fff;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e2da;
  }
  .source-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .source-label {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: #0f2742;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
  }
  .source-desc {
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: #6b7280;
  }
  .source-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: #b22234;
    text-decoration: none;
    word-break: break-all;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .source-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .todo-link {
    color: #b45309;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .source-note {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: #6b7280;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .responsible-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .responsible-list li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: #374151;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .responsible-list li::before {
    content: "•";
    color: #c68a4a;
    font-weight: 700;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
</style>
